1:  82c9e77 ! 1:  41e37c2 release: automate maintained packages with GitHub Actions
    @@ Metadata
      ## Commit message ##
         release: automate maintained packages with GitHub Actions
     
    -    Build and test the maintained server and clients from tagged source, then
    -    publish their retained artifacts after GitHub environment approval. Use
    -    trusted registry credentials, verify existing versions during recovery,
    -    and synchronize the PHP mirror over scoped SSH access.
    +    Build and retain the maintained packages in one validated Actions run,
    +    then publish those artifacts after protected-environment approval. Use
    +    trusted registry credentials and a scoped PHP deploy key, with immutable
    +    version checks and recovery from partial publication.
     
    -    Keep build-only verification available for release tooling changes and
    -    exclude Elixir from all release operations. Preserve package identities
    -    and the existing shared-version release-branch policy.
    +    Backport the release tooling while retaining release-line tests and
    +    server-shell dependencies. Pin the current Nix setup action patch for its
    +    upstream security fix.
    +
    +    (cherry picked from commit 82c9e778d04e0228785413a515e9ca76b2956215)
     
